{%- comment -%}
Small institution crest, sized to sit inline with body text.
Usage: {% include inst_logo.liquid file="unc.svg" alt="UNC Chapel Hill" %}

`bust_file_cache` appends an MD5 of the file, so swapping a crest actually reaches
visitors instead of leaving them on a browser-cached copy of the old one.

This file deliberately ends without a trailing newline: Jekyll emits an include
verbatim, so a final newline would render as a stray space between the crest and
whatever punctuation follows it.
{%- endcomment -%}<img class="inst-logo" src="{{ '/assets/img/logos/' | append: include.file | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}" alt="{{ include.alt }}" title="{{ include.alt }}">